MTP history lookup on the V2 model runner.

The lookup shipped first in the V1 proposer (`mtp-history-lookup.patch`,
`VLLM_MTP_LOOKUP`). vLLM 0.29 defaults to the V2 runner, whose MTP speculator
proposes its own block; this adds the same feature there, matching against the
runner's `all_token_ids` history, which is current at propose() time. The same
gate applies (the step that just finished accepted every draft it was given,
the previous match was long enough, and this match can fill the whole block),
all decided on device with no host synchronization; an overridden request's
draft distribution becomes a point mass on the proposed token, which is a legal
q for rejection sampling, so the output distribution is unchanged. Greedy only
unless `VLLM_MTP_LOOKUP_SAMPLED=1`, like V1, and disabled when the draft
vocabulary is not the target vocabulary (the lookup proposes target ids).

Measured on the 2080 Ti, V2 runner, k=4, 32k-word verbatim copy, 512 output
tokens: acceptance 4.19-4.22 and 107.1-107.9 tok/s against the V2 baseline's
3.66-3.84 and 93.8-98.0, and V1+lookup's 3.73-3.93 and 96.3-101.5. Prose is at
parity (8k acceptance 3.969, 117.7/113.5 tok/s; 32k 3.97, 101.9), sampled
traffic is untouched (the lookup is gated off), and GSM8K n=100 reads 94.0%
against the deployed stack's 94.5% (n=200).

